1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[narrator] After he parts ways with Killua

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
in order to stop the sorting process,

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Gon finds himself under attack
by new Chimera Ants.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
[Gon] An owl and a bat?

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
They're both nocturnal creatures.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Hunters of the night.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Bring it.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,000
[groans]

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The owl's feathers?

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,000
The bat's wings are so loud,
I couldn't hear the owl coming.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
[opening theme music playing]

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
[singer singing in English]

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

15
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
[singer singing in English]

16
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

17
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
COMBINATION X AND X EVOLUTION

18
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
[Owl Ant laughs]
My ears can pick up sounds

19
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
-[wings flapping loudly]
-[Gon] From the right this time.

20
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,000
[groans]

21
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[Bat Ant] All that aura
still won't help you.

22
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
We rule the darkness.

23
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
[Gon] I need a new approach.

24
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
If the owl is acting as backup,

25
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
I've gotta focus on the sound
of the bat's wings.

26
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
[loud flapping]

27
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Right after the owl attacks,
the bat strikes.

28
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,000
-[wings flap]
-Now.

29
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
[gasps] I missed?
But my timing was perfect.

30
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Is it echolocation?

31
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Damn. I missed again?

32
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:31,000
[Bat Ant] He's correctly guessing
the direction of my attacks.

33
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
[Gon] It seems the bat uses echolocation

34
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:45,000
to anticipate the timing
and angle of my attack.

35
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
[Owl Ant] Can I assist?

36
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:15,000
[Bat Ant] Hold on. I'll try
getting closer as quietly as I can.

37
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
It's all gone.

38
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,000
[Bat Ant] Now without flapping.

39
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
-A Dive Bomb!
-[Gon] No way.

40
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Your wings are nothing like the owl's,

41
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
so I can hear you
slicing through the air as you fall.

42
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,000
[Bat Ant] Well, go on.
Show me your ultimate attack.

43
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
No reaction? [laughs]

44
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Pathetic human ears.

45
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,000
[Bat Ant gasps] That noise! I can't see.

46
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,000
I have to escape.

47
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Not so fast.

48
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:15,000
but when it comes to attacking with sound,
I can't be beat.

49
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
[Meleoron] This is why
they're such a great team.

50
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,000
They strike with sound
and finish with brawn.

51
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
[laughs]

52
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Well, kid?

53
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
[Gon] Do I plug my ears? No.

54
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:32,000
If I limit my hearing,
my reaction time will suffer.

55
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
I know. Gyo.

56
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:37,000
[Owl Ant] Huh? Glowing eyes?

57
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,000
No, it's aura.

58
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
He's focusing on sight instead of hearing.

59
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,000
[Bat Ant] Let's give him another.

60
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Nauseating Noise!

61
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,000
[grunts]

62
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Water significantly weakens
the energy of sound.

63
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,000
-[high-pitched ringing]
-[Gon groaning]

64
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
when stalking their prey.

65
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,000
they'll take me down
before I can even find them.

66
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:55,000
[Meleoron] In terms of latent aura,
this kid has a clear advantage.

67
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Even after all those hits,
he's still unharmed.

68
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,000
But his capability is irrelevant.

69
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:05,000
Without a strategy,
he's just a moving target.

70
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:16,000
[Owl Ant] The fool must think that
staying really close to me all the time

71
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
will prevent the sonic attacks.

72
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
[Bat Ant] No such luck.

73
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
-[high-pitched ringing]
-[groaning]

74
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
If I use Rock, I know can defeat this one,

75
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:28,000
but if I do, the bat might run off
and warn the other Ants.

76
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:34,000
[Owl Ant laughs]
To me, a starry night is as bright as day.

77
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
As long as I'm not in pitch darkness,

78
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:41,000
I can see you
without needing to rely on my hearing.

79
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,000
That means that if I cover my ears…

80
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
[Meleoron] So the kid has shrouded
his entire body in aura

81
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
to avoid major damage.

82
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:59,000
But that greatly reduces
the strength of his attacks,

83
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:02,000
making it impossible
to stand against them.

84
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Here!

85
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
They always take positions
on opposite sides

86
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
to avoid both being targeted at once.

87
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,000
…the bat is behind me.

88
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Then the real wall was behind me.

89
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
[Owl Ant] He turned our teamwork
against us?

90
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[gasps]

91
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Damn! [panting]

92
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,000
-[Gon] Show me Rock!
-Huh?

93
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
-Janken…
-Why, you…

94
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
-[gasps]
-Rock!

95
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,000
[gasps]

96
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
[Gon] I made sure to knock you west.

97
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Go back to the NGL!

98
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
[Meleoron] That was incredible.

99
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:47,000
I see. So that's his signature move.

100
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
I take it back. He can be useful.

101
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
But how do I proceed?

102
00:10:55,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Diego's been dethroned,
and now soldiers, all of them brainwashed,

103
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Can't be.

104
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,000
We all saw the soldiers
try to kill everyone.

105
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Warn the people in other areas. Go! Hurry!

106
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Meow, it was from the southeast this time.

107
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
Some of my puppets have been stopped.

108
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
He's fast.

109
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Well, whoever they are,
they're unpredictable.

110
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,000
An assassin?

111
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
But it seems like
they're acting on their own.

112
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,000
A decoy?

113
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
[groans] This is so annoying.

114
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
I wanna kill them!

115
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
[violin music playing]

116
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:07,000
[Shaiapouf] It may all be
an act to draw you out,

117
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:17,000
My anguish is intoxicating
as I wallow in my dilemma.

118
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
[Shaiapouf] The answer is quite simple.

119
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Our duty is to protect the King.

120
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:33,000
We must focus on that
and let the other Ants handle the rest.

121
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,000
[door opens]

122
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
[Leol] Is it our turn?

123
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:43,000
When we were injured and on the run
from the Hunters, you took us in,

124
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Someone is out there
running around and disabling my puppets.

125
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
Can you go and kill them?

126
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
[Leol] You can count on me.

127
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Perfect. Take this.

128
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,000
We can't use telepathy, you see.

129
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
That's how I'll give you updates
on their location.

130
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,000
[Leol] Right.

131
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:31,000
we can be sure that they'll be
working hard to carry out their mission.

132
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:36,000
[Shaiapouf] However,
they may be waiting to betray us.

133
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
[chuckles] And in that case,

134
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,000
[Killua panting]

135
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
The closest village to here
is at two o'clock,

136
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
and the next ones are at eight and ten.

137
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Should I just skip them and head for Taba,
40 kilometers away?

138
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,000
[Knuckle groans] This is bad.

139
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Must have slipped past
the Hunters that replaced us.

140
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Not bad,

141
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:10,000
but Colt has confirmed that unfortunately
none of them were squadron leaders.

142
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:15,000
According to him, there are eight of them
left that would be considered aggressive.

143
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,000
They've encountered four so far,

144
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,000
but every last one of them was
able to avoid being killed or captured.

145
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Cheetu is going to East Gorteau
for a reason.

146
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,000
I'm willing to bet that
he knows the King is there.

147
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:31,000
I'm positive he's choosing
to return to the service of the King

148
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
in order to increase his own power.

149
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,000
My ability is still in effect
for the time being,

150
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:39,000
and I'm a lot stronger than he is,

151
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,000
but if we let him slip away from us

152
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,000
and he can gain even more power
before we meet again,

153
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
then all bets are off.

154
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:49,000
Plus if we allow any more Ants like him
to join up with the King's forces,

155
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:53,000
then we'll never be able
to draw the Royal Guard away.

156
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Still wanna stop me? Do your best.

157
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
But I'm not gonna make it easy for you.

158
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Uh…

159
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,000
First we should contact Mr. Morel.

160
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
If worse comes to worst,

161
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,000
he'll need to have adequate time
to find replacements for us.

162
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
I'm coming with you.

163
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,000
This should increase the odds
of us capturing that Ant.

164
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,000
[chuckles]

165
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
It's Knuckle. Something's come up.

166
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Yes, I guess so. Probably.

167
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,000
[Morel] Fools!

168
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
I thought I told you to send Likke.

169
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
There's no one
more suited for this than him.

170
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Huh?

171
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:55,000
Guess the review board didn't send over
the Hunter that we requested.

172
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
And who did they send instead?

173
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Some Hunter I've never heard of,
probably just a temp.

174
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,000
A temp?

175
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,000
You mean hired Hunters
who only take assigned jobs

176
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
through the Hunter Association?

177
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Not surprisingly, they have less talent.

178
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Damn it!

179
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,000
I should have just
gone to talk to Likke myself.

180
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Come on now. Stop being so foolish.

181
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Bear in mind
that if we go over the board's head,

182
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:24,000
the Chairman is the one who's going to get
saddled with all of the blame.

183
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,000
He had to argue with the board
just to get us here.

184
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,000
I can't imagine it would go well for him.

185
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Yeah, but they don't understand
the situation here.

186
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:39,000
It's based on donations
and who did what way back when.

187
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Yes, but that's no surprise.
The board has always been inflexible.

188
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,000
How the hell can you be so relaxed, huh?

189
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,000
If we underestimate the squadron leaders,
we'll pay dearly for it.

190
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Fact of the matter is
these things are tough,

191
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:20,000
that the Vice-Chairman's faction
is bribing the board?

192
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,000
Is that right?

193
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:33,000
There's no evidence of that happening.

194
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
[laughs] You think
they're stupid enough to get caught?

195
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
Look at the facts.

196
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,000
The squadron leaders,

197
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,000
every single one of them they've faced,
has escaped alive.

198
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:48,000
If we don't succeed,
the Chairman will be blamed.

199
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
He'll take the fall for everything.

200
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:55,000
The Vice-Chairman's supporters
will do anything to guarantee that.

201
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,000
The more victims the Ants claim,

202
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:00,000
the louder the voices
screaming for his resignation.

203
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Meanwhile, they're just kicking back
in their office chairs.

204
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
[Knov] Hmm.

205
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
If we can take out the King,

206
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:12,000
but five million people are already dead,
then we've totally failed!

207
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:22,000
When he devised this plan,
he was fully aware of the consequences.

208
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:26,000
He knew exactly how much time
assuring victory would take

209
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
and how many casualties.

210
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:32,000
[Morel grunts angrily]
Five million's on the low end.

211
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,000
That's still too high.

212
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
[cell phone ringing]

213
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,000
[Morel] Mr. Marcos?

214
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,000
What?

215
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:47,000
[Marcos] The damn phones
have been ringing nonstop.

216
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:51,000
And that's not all.
Rumors of a coup d'état are flying around.

217
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:55,000
It's been discovered that mass murders
are taking place all over the country.

218
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:58,000
It's no rumor.
I mean, it's actually happening.

219
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
What is going on here?

220
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Tell me, are you responsible?

221
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:04,000
We haven't done anything.

222
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Did the public find out about the sorting?

223
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,000
-[alarm blaring]
-[gasps] We'll talk later on.

224
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:14,000
-Now go back to your office immediately.
-[Knov] Morel.

225
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,000
-Huh?
-[line disconnects]

226
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Good evening. The dearly beloved
leader of our land, Diego,

227
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
has an urgent announcement to make.

228
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,000
[over speaker]
To ensure our great leader's message

229
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:25,000
will be heard clearly
throughout the nation,

230
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
we request that
all relay speakers in all regions

231
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,000
be turned to maximum volume.

232
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
All televisions and radios should be on

233
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,000
and the volume raised
to its maximum setting.

234
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:52,000
that would foment rebellion.

235
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,000
I ask you not to leave your residence
for any reason.

236
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Lock your doors.

237
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:15,000
The soldiers of my special forces
will soon be visiting your residences

238
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,000
That happened too quickly.

239
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,000
It would give them
all the excuse they needed

240
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,000
[slow pop music playing]

241
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:03,000
[scoffs] Yeah, bring it on.

242
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Tanks, jets,
whatever the hell else you've got.

243
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[upbeat music playing]

244
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:33,000
[Gon] Next time, "Tracking and Pursuit."

245
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:34,000
-Ninety-eight…
-[Killua] Ninety-nine…

246
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,000
-[both] One hundred!
-[Gon] Thanks, everyone.

247
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:39,000
[Killua] For helping us reach
100 episodes.
